.TH "GF-DATASOURCES-DELETE-DATASOURCE-BY-UID" "1" "May 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-datasources-delete-datasource-by-uid - Deletes an existing data source by UID


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf datasources delete-datasource-by-uid [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes an existing data source by UID

.PP
If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled you need to have a permission with action: \fBdatasources:delete\fR and scopes: \fBdatasources:*\fR, \fBdatasources:uid:*\fR and \fBdatasources:uid:kLtEtcRGk\fR (single data source).

.PP
Response schema (DeleteDataSourceByUIDOK.Payload):
  message  string


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--describe-response-jsonschema\fP[=false]
	Print the JSON Schema of the response payload and exit without calling the API

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for delete-datasource-by-uid

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	Print the raw HTTP response body instead of the decoded payload

.PP
\fB--uid\fP=""
	UID [required]


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
